Chapter 8: Sliding Window vs Two Pointers

This is where many students get confused.

Sliding Window

Window always represents one continuous segment.

[L.........R]

You're maintaining a valid window.

Two Pointers

Pointers don't necessarily represent a window.

They can

Move toward each other
Move independently
Work on different arrays
Scan a string from both ends

Example

Palindrome

a b c b a
↑       ↑

No window.

Just comparison.

